# Coding Standards — GeoGebra AutoDraw AI

> Mandatory standards for all code in this project. Read alongside `specs/README.md`.

## Language convention
- Files under `specs/` are written in **Vietnamese**.
- Every other file (code, comments, UI strings, error messages, prompt templates, `.md`, JSON, configs) is written in **English** — including user-facing UI strings.

## Architecture
- Functional components (React), no class components.
- Clean Architecture / SOLID: separate UI, business logic, and I/O (chrome API).
- Distributed extension: do NOT mix Popup / Background / Content logic. One `src/` folder per environment.
- Message-passing types are centralized in `src/shared/messages.ts`. Do not hardcode `action` strings around the codebase.

## Language & formatting
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` (use `unknown` + narrow when needed).
- Keep code concise, split into small functions, name things clearly.
- Comments: explain "why" only, do not restate what the code already says.

## Error handling
- Wrap every chrome API / async business call in `try-catch`.
- Wrap `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` to guard against "Extension context invalidated".
- A single `evalCommand` failure must NOT stop the batch — collect into `errors[]` (spec §10).
- Log errors explicitly, return normalized messages to the UI.

## Testing (TDD)
- Write tests before feature code (Vitest).
- Tests required for: `sanitize`, prompt generation, history reducer.
- Pure logic (no chrome API dependency) must be split out so it stays testable.

## Chrome Extension
- Manifest V3. Two-layer content script: ISOLATED (message passing) + MAIN (ggbApplet.evalCommand), bridged via `window.postMessage` (spec §7.2).
- No unnecessary permissions. Currently only `tabs`, `storage`.
